  "page1": {
    "title": "The Tiny Living World",
    "subtitle": "Meet the small living things that share our world.",
    "body": "Tiny living things are all around us. Some of them are too small to see. We call these little ones microbes.\n\nMold and mushrooms are fungi. They grow on old bread and on damp trees. Bacteria are even smaller than fungi. They live in soil, in water, and inside our bodies. A paramecium swims and spins in pond water.\n\nMany microbes help us each day. Some bacteria <mark>turn milk into yogurt</mark>. They also help us make doenjang. Fungi even give us useful medicine.\n\nMicrobes break down dead leaves in the ground. This keeps the soil clean and rich. But some microbes can make us sick. So we wash our hands well every day.",
    "illustration": "assets/illustrations/mars/2026-07/16.jpg",
    "illustration_caption": "Mold and mushrooms, tiny bacteria, and a paramecium — the small living world all around us.",
